<section id="difference" class="section intro">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">A DIFFERENT KIND OF SMART</p>
    <h2>
      All the connection.
      <br />
      <em>None of the dependency.</em>
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="lead">Your introduction shouldn’t depend on a signal.</p>
    <p>
    Many smart business cards store a web address that opens an online profile,
    where the recipient can view your details. Cardistry takes a different
    route: your contact information is stored directly on the NFC chip, rather
    than relying on a hosted profile to display it.
    </p>

    <p>
      With a compatible NFC reader and supported contact format, those details
      can be read directly from the card without an internet connection.
      While the QR gives recipients another way to access your details using a
      compatible smartphone camera or QR scanner. All this without needing to tap the
      NFC chip or load an online profile.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>
        Your details travel with your card, not just with a link to a website.
      </strong>
      <br> Reading directly stored information can <strong>work offline</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
    On a compatible phone, your details can be read without fetching a web page. Less
    friction between “nice to meet you” and “let’s stay in touch”.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
